INT. GENERATION SHIP "ANAMNESIS" - COUNCIL CHAMBER - SHIP DAY

A circular hall with a ceiling like the inside of a seed. Six seats are arranged around a table of pale resin. The viewport behind them shows stars drifting in a very slow river.

ELDER TOMOKO VASQUEZ-ADEBAYO (70s, high collar, white hair braided to her waist) sits at the head. NAVIGATOR PRIYADARSHINI OKEKE (40s, ink-stained fingers, silent) sits beside her. MEDIC CORVIN HALLORAN-NWOSU (50s, round glasses, a satchel of vials) leans forward. ENGINEER BEATRIX SOLBERG-MWANGI (30s, rolled sleeves, calloused hands) sits scowling with her arms crossed. ARCHIVIST DESMOND OYELARAN-PIKE (60s, tweed, a book on his knee) sits very upright. And at the foot, the youngest, ZANELE KOROMA-LINDEN (20s, council apprentice, uniform too stiff) holds a stylus above a slate.

TOMOKO
We begin.

PRIYADARSHINI
Fuel reserves?

BEATRIX
Eleven percent.

PRIYADARSHINI
Eleven.

BEATRIX
Eleven and falling.

CORVIN
The farm decks are failing too.

DESMOND
That is in the records.

CORVIN
The records do not feed anyone.

DESMOND
They tell us why.

CORVIN
Why does not matter. When does.

TOMOKO
Please.

They quiet. Zanele writes.

TOMOKO (CONT'D)
We will decide today whether the ship turns.

BEATRIX
Turning costs four percent.

PRIYADARSHINI
Not turning costs everything.

DESMOND
There is a system two light-years aft.

BEATRIX
Two years of burn.

DESMOND
Two years of burn, and a green world.

CORVIN
How green?

DESMOND
Not as green as the book.

CORVIN
Then how green?

DESMOND
Enough.

Zanele raises her stylus.

ZANELE
May I speak?

TOMOKO
The apprentice speaks last.

ZANELE
Yes, Elder.

TOMOKO
But speak.

ZANELE
If we turn, my children will be born in the turn.

BEATRIX
So?

ZANELE
So they will never see where we were going.

DESMOND
They will see where we got.

ZANELE
Is that enough?

Nobody answers. Tomoko rests her palms on the resin and closes her eyes. Priyadarshini studies her own inked fingers. Corvin pulls a vial from his satchel, then puts it back. Beatrix uncrosses her arms.

BEATRIX
I would turn.

CORVIN
I would turn.

DESMOND
Archives will log it.

PRIYADARSHINI
Turn.

TOMOKO
Then it is decided.

ZANELE
(whispering)
Thank you.

TOMOKO
Do not thank us. Remember us.

She taps the table. The stars in the viewport shift. A deep note vibrates through the floor, and the entire ship begins to bank, so slowly that only the stars know.
